canonical_claim.statement:
Corrected statement. Under the standing assumptions, let $f(\mathbf{X_i},\theta_{\mathbf{i}})$ be any real-valued random variables on the assignment space (they may depend on the realized assignment, for instance through a data-derived $\theta_{\mathbf{i}}$). Then:
(a) eq. [17], corrected: $\mathrm{E}\left[\widehat{Y_1^{T*}}\right] = \mathrm{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}T_i\frac{Y_{1i}}{\pi_{1i}} - \sum_{i=1}^{N}T_i\frac{f(\mathbf{X_i},\theta_{\mathbf{i}})}{\pi_{1i}} + \sum_{i=1}^{N}f(\mathbf{X_i},\theta_{\mathbf{i}})\right] = Y_1^T - \sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathrm{Cov}\left(T_i,\frac{f(\mathbf{X_i},\theta_{\mathbf{i}})}{\pi_{1i}}\right)$;
(b) eq. [18], 'and, likewise,': $\mathrm{E}\left[\widehat{Y_0^{T*}}\right] = Y_0^T - \sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathrm{Cov}\left((1-T_i),\frac{f(\mathbf{X_i},\theta_{\mathbf{i}})}{\pi_{0i}}\right)$;
(c) eq. [19], 'In general, the bias of the estimator based on eqs. [13] and [14] will therefore be': $\mathrm{E}\left[\widehat{\Delta_G}\right] - \Delta = \frac{1}{N}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathrm{Cov}\left((1-T_i),\frac{f(\mathbf{X_i},\theta_{\mathbf{i}})}{\pi_{0i}}\right) - \sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathrm{Cov}\left(T_i,\frac{f(\mathbf{X_i},\theta_{\mathbf{i}})}{\pi_{1i}}\right)\right)$.
